+
+Installed Supabase CLI 2.117.0 created `20261115162257_ai_budget_all_caller_sources.sql` with empty HOME and network denial. The forward migration extends registration to legacy qualitative, A12 canonical rewrite, A13 initial feedback and account-only Build. Legacy rewrite input/OP2 bytes remain unchanged. Qualitative retains its real server analysis UUID; A13 retains its actual server operation UUID. Existing unregistered R03 rows cannot be adopted retrospectively. A12 derives its technical ID from owner/org/analysis/version/client-operation scope while preserving its public typed operation ID, policy and receipt. Build derives account-scoped OP2; its three parent selectors are literal NULL. All retained ambiguous OP1/raw-ID collisions refuse new admission, irrespective of accounting state.
+
+Atomic source reservation proves the actual parent and typed context before calling a service-denied private ordinal helper. A13 requires its real prepared operation, reserved attempt, ordinal, policy/token tuple and active lease through the unchanged strict Native validator. Lease and attempt proof do not enter immutable operation identity or export. A12 requires its full scoped private operation, binding/model/prompt and deterministic technical attempt. Build requires actual Auth/org/membership and durable owner admission; it is never selected by resume-root retirement.
+
+Generic public reserve, reserve-next and claim deny registered A12/A13 kinds. Their private gate first takes the existing exclusive owner mutex without waiting, then reads the durable barrier and source kind in separate volatile commands. Source registration holds shared admission in that same lock domain, so registration cannot race classification through the transition. Typed claims reach the private technical transition only after their existing once/source/lease/consent/policy checks. No caller flag or GUC grants authority. The original private budget arithmetic, periods, settlement, unknown holds, reconciliation and predispatch release remain unchanged.
+
+Capture and export consume exact registrations. Build uses account preparation and NULL-safe disposition matching; other kinds keep exact root selectors and the original minimum account/root clock. Source export advances explicitly to version 2 with the same ten fields, full owner scope, 4,096-row/32-MiB bounds and exact ledger join. A13 lease/attempt fields are excluded. Registration time never becomes a deletion clock. Metadata retains nine keys, six profile strings and independent denied data capabilities.
+
+Twenty guarded body replacements and seven private helpers form the successor. The source checker binds 48 actual function digests/properties, current typed admission and the exact catalogue. Before any ALTER, installation locks the relevant tables, verifies the old checker digest and requires old source readiness. It then initializes a new metadata-only seal once. The old closed seal is neither updated nor resealed; its closed trigger is fingerprinted, while only the new bootstrap trigger is omitted before installation. Six Node profile modules carry actual postimage digests. Stored policy JSON, legacy scoring and historical migrations are unchanged.
